[{:db/id "q-81145/selection/56a65eb57c48ed997515ad7e6c46c49f3b1746773e228af09678b0e781bc8916" :answer/id #uuid "448d0e50-fa7e-5a83-8011-6a32f858f1ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =-2\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81145/selection/ced5f03a13766b543177494be249d2141f428fe5d80d773d49bebb0eebfc1f7a" :answer/id #uuid "c19d0ef4-e635-5bf8-ba49-b3a57949282e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =2\\pm 4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81145/selection/b156ddeac36ef28ba74e9326d38b8eab0cde4bc577d49261f9c6dc352c0abad8" :answer/id #uuid "01447c0b-3378-57ac-bd6d-940812e6297d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =4\\pm 4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81145/selection/47ee0fb1fc99fb4702b5f5fe47ba4a74ec35f652ce0100885b8cdfc06d517ee4" :answer/id #uuid "b6ce7ead-3ca1-55de-ae44-031bb1d5acc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =2\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81145/selection/d05ec8183967564373c16b1236086fc3ba2a155253ddc086af441892798fac74" :answer/id #uuid "908c641c-8c75-5747-b97d-4a7066c4209b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =-4\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81145/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "abea00d8-86be-57e0-9341-bef90d003d03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81145/selection/47ee0fb1fc99fb4702b5f5fe47ba4a74ec35f652ce0100885b8cdfc06d517ee4" :answer-field/choices ["q-81145/selection/56a65eb57c48ed997515ad7e6c46c49f3b1746773e228af09678b0e781bc8916" "q-81145/selection/ced5f03a13766b543177494be249d2141f428fe5d80d773d49bebb0eebfc1f7a" "q-81145/selection/b156ddeac36ef28ba74e9326d38b8eab0cde4bc577d49261f9c6dc352c0abad8" "q-81145/selection/47ee0fb1fc99fb4702b5f5fe47ba4a74ec35f652ce0100885b8cdfc06d517ee4" "q-81145/selection/d05ec8183967564373c16b1236086fc3ba2a155253ddc086af441892798fac74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81145" :question/id #uuid "52a1a1aa-514c-57f9-bd39-ce5bd13a5f16" :question/math-academy-id "q-81145" :question/problem "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 13 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 13 \\\\ -1 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 13 \\\\ -1 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-13(-1) & =0 \\\\ -5-5\\lambda +\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+13 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(1)(8)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =2\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81145/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a453400-6363-5782-b346-aae37570c9bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81145"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102774/selection/5c003b440922104cdb1c59955f7400755ab2b118591a28c3be31ceeb70a3750e" :answer/id #uuid "94428639-dc50-54e9-b416-dd2cdee43064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102774/selection/baa80a8068dd7c782dcda3a7ea56c67dd55cb5cc6dc80a1fdbf0bd1389d0e657" :answer/id #uuid "682cd574-a2ce-5e59-87eb-120649e0e0d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102774/selection/7a1edb636192bac13d526950c590a28e6420617b7e881f4b588d8ed84ba80b22" :answer/id #uuid "83b22e43-8a04-5b1f-be5d-2a48bf25c3c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =1\\pm 3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102774/selection/3003ce2317913d3e83a7e3871731a0ea3b324e232f4bda76ca63ca13482684f6" :answer/id #uuid "900a350d-e84a-57fe-a9cb-a68205b096f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102774/selection/9d4820f181a4cf2ffd0e3c6eae8626e87b7ced6cdbf315cc346fe8ed5bc90b43" :answer/id #uuid "c0037e85-cc20-5185-910b-6e8865d8ea7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =2\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102774/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d07b967-8c6a-5044-b195-1a849b9b2b7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102774/selection/5c003b440922104cdb1c59955f7400755ab2b118591a28c3be31ceeb70a3750e" :answer-field/choices ["q-102774/selection/5c003b440922104cdb1c59955f7400755ab2b118591a28c3be31ceeb70a3750e" "q-102774/selection/baa80a8068dd7c782dcda3a7ea56c67dd55cb5cc6dc80a1fdbf0bd1389d0e657" "q-102774/selection/7a1edb636192bac13d526950c590a28e6420617b7e881f4b588d8ed84ba80b22" "q-102774/selection/3003ce2317913d3e83a7e3871731a0ea3b324e232f4bda76ca63ca13482684f6" "q-102774/selection/9d4820f181a4cf2ffd0e3c6eae8626e87b7ced6cdbf315cc346fe8ed5bc90b43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102774" :question/id #uuid "b2011979-5619-5433-8ebc-20f4b5c10550" :question/math-academy-id "q-102774" :question/problem "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(-1)(3) & =0 \\\\ 1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(4)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102774/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a453400-6363-5782-b346-aae37570c9bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102774"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81020/selection/e3c1b58920f85a5f0b5ecd33563b3956a5ec398d534516cbb849461b63bc9df3" :answer/id #uuid "4dcf64c8-0e9c-5b2d-b83b-bd144b8aa6a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81020/selection/9dc9e32e8c07cb55713aac967947119eba89184004a29831ec6bd66540436519" :answer/id #uuid "75b1c6ad-a4ff-5af0-ac92-c3a2dfb11a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =1\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81020/selection/7304e45403a258c572b59ea9b6c5a54f20b0c097a2fea2754d132cebe6963d30" :answer/id #uuid "5b320076-6a1a-5a47-b1fa-33cad5728cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =-1\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81020/selection/50b01111532f868128cca79dfde5f2933be130afa073f8460e724815b5345c99" :answer/id #uuid "c646025c-3970-5383-b10f-963b861997c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81020/selection/4b165438449e230f8f7e9d896c3d6ef498e4cdb797ae0a6da31fd5fa60775c10" :answer/id #uuid "d91f4833-ab35-5632-add8-1ba4e5ff1008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81020/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a164f5c-ae78-598a-b9be-c4007d16fee4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81020/selection/4b165438449e230f8f7e9d896c3d6ef498e4cdb797ae0a6da31fd5fa60775c10" :answer-field/choices ["q-81020/selection/e3c1b58920f85a5f0b5ecd33563b3956a5ec398d534516cbb849461b63bc9df3" "q-81020/selection/9dc9e32e8c07cb55713aac967947119eba89184004a29831ec6bd66540436519" "q-81020/selection/7304e45403a258c572b59ea9b6c5a54f20b0c097a2fea2754d132cebe6963d30" "q-81020/selection/50b01111532f868128cca79dfde5f2933be130afa073f8460e724815b5345c99" "q-81020/selection/4b165438449e230f8f7e9d896c3d6ef498e4cdb797ae0a6da31fd5fa60775c10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81020" :question/id #uuid "0c2c99cf-c3a7-50b6-b9ac-8b79e22cca54" :question/math-academy-id "q-81020" :question/problem "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-1(-2) & =0 \\\\ -1-\\lambda +\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81020/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a453400-6363-5782-b346-aae37570c9bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81020"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81034/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "9623a387-dcc5-5ff2-a5c4-b8069eaeedac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81034/selection/5b5c2c39549080b8852cc601b2734981074ad223caceae684f2cd70ca44c91a4" :answer/id #uuid "9156e141-e86e-5623-963c-e0e0a82c25d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81034/selection/a292c43a5bdd99f5ad91dc2c1ffcf1365e0f66bcc30237684298c4592b5a76aa" :answer/id #uuid "b76e2b90-842a-51ef-9483-3a8edd3c6e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81034/selection/dfa79ea8c0f005d192a25bc3d73b55a3e4817ec79c17e182c6efc0ffdc1e3e15" :answer/id #uuid "4394758e-5885-5bba-ad8b-7fb1fe42f4ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81034/selection/6115cec4c91996e51c6f66aac3fdd66c7ac2a5d2d6833fb5c44157bd1ea74b91" :answer/id #uuid "4177b88d-1042-5157-a96f-6f401b02cb81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81034/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb17ee37-b786-528f-8f49-e6df624e0be5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81034/selection/6115cec4c91996e51c6f66aac3fdd66c7ac2a5d2d6833fb5c44157bd1ea74b91" :answer-field/choices ["q-81034/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-81034/selection/5b5c2c39549080b8852cc601b2734981074ad223caceae684f2cd70ca44c91a4" "q-81034/selection/a292c43a5bdd99f5ad91dc2c1ffcf1365e0f66bcc30237684298c4592b5a76aa" "q-81034/selection/dfa79ea8c0f005d192a25bc3d73b55a3e4817ec79c17e182c6efc0ffdc1e3e15" "q-81034/selection/6115cec4c91996e51c6f66aac3fdd66c7ac2a5d2d6833fb5c44157bd1ea74b91"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81034" :question/id #uuid "715463ab-9e05-5a99-9ffd-e4ae937011d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-81034" :question/problem "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=5-6\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $\\frac{1}{4}({\\lambda }_{1}-{\\lambda }_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=5-6\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=5+6\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}({\\lambda }_{1}-{\\lambda }_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{4}(5-6\\text{i}-(5+6\\text{i})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(-12\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81034/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eae4328-dd7c-5f77-8958-840cadb6f7f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39184"] :question/problem "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+2\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $2({\\lambda }_{2}-{\\lambda }_{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+2\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=4-2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({\\lambda }_{2}-{\\lambda }_{1}) & =2(4-2\\text{i}-(4+2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(-4\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5904"] :question/problem "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/assets/61d1e4670c482f79d4b87ff36bb772339a704df18ccfb624ce183729f5022c4c.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/assets/8bfd617b360f6bed1fcf835ebe52c56f3c7b6a5a5234e099f7a0aec0d4bbdc36.png)\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2(-2) & =0 \\\\ 1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(5)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=1\\pm 2\\textrm{i}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
